
# .cursor/rules/entity-framework.mdc

## Rule: DbContext Usage
- Do not instantiate DbContext directly; use dependency injection.
- Respect existing OnModelCreating configurations.

## Rule: Migrations
- Do not generate or apply EF Core migrations unless asked.
- Never remove existing migrations.

## Rule: Asynchronous Code
- Prefer async methods (e.g., ToListAsync, SaveChangesAsync) for DB operations.
- Do not mix async and sync calls in the same method.

## Rule: Tracking and Performance
- Use .AsNoTracking() for read-only queries.
- Avoid loading large datasets into memory unnecessarily.

## Rule: Relationship Mapping
- Preserve existing relationships (One-to-Many, Many-to-Many) unless asked to modify.
- When defining navigation properties, configure both sides clearly.
